{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The pain on the tendon is usually related to the flexor tendons in the fingers, which attach to muscles in the forearms that pull on the tendons, bend the fingers, and allow us to crimp. The pain on the pulley is usually related to the annular pulleys (A1, A2, A3, A4, and A5), which keep the tendon close to the bone when bending the fingers. The pain on the joint is usually related to the ligaments that connect and stabilize the bones. Since you mentioned that the pain could be on the tendon, I would recommend checking if you have any damage to the flexor tendons or the annular pulleys. It's also possible that you have a muscle strain, which can occur when the muscles in the forearms are fatigued and you're trying to crimp. If you're experiencing pain on the tendon, it's a good idea to consult with a medical professional to get a proper diagnosis", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:1": 715.2482299804688, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:2": 715.09912109375, "clueweb22-en0015-71-10781:17": 714.7743530273438, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:0": 714.7621459960938, "clueweb22-en0015-71-10781:16": 714.7213134765625}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors.", "Many years ago I had a bad fall while bouldering."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:1": 715.2482299804688, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:2": 715.09912109375, "clueweb22-en0015-71-10781:17": 714.7743530273438, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:0": 714.7621459960938, "clueweb22-en0015-71-10781:16": 714.7213134765625, "clueweb22-en0040-26-09986:2": 714.5543823242188, "clueweb22-en0013-93-15759:18": 714.5439453125, "clueweb22-en0016-25-19413:13": 714.5439453125, "clueweb22-en0038-00-07527:13": 714.543212890625, "clueweb22-en0030-70-18403:1": 714.53369140625, "clueweb22-en0023-29-16320:5": 714.4823608398438, "clueweb22-en0030