{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The subway is the lifeblood of the city, without it, the city grinds to a halt. It connects New Yorkers of all races and incomes and drives the city\u2019s economic booms. People think of the subway as the lifeblood of the city, and it\u2019s especially unfair to essential workers who depend on it to get to work. The subway was more important than ever to the people who took it throughout the pandemic, and all New Yorkers who depended on their ability to get to work. Even if only thousands of people were commuting at that particular time, in essence millions were depending on that commute. The subway has never been segregated, it is always open, and the fare is always the same no matter how far you need to go. In New York, movement \u2014 anywhere, anytime \u2014 is a right. Most countries treat subway systems as national assets. The subway has no zones and no hours of operation. It brings people together, but it also spreads people out. It is this paradox", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0020-81-12610:3": 712.8626708984375, "clueweb22-en0041-95-06774:10": 712.6270751953125, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:3": 712.6218872070312, "clueweb22-en0020-81-12610:2": 712.4979858398438, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:6": 712.424560546875}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0020-81-12610:3": 712.8626708984375, "clueweb22-en0041-95-06774:10": 712.6270751953125, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:3": 712.6218872070312, "clueweb22-en0020-81-12610:2": 712.4979858398438, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:6": 712.424560546875, "clueweb22-en0034-30-02400:5": 712.3246459960938, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:4": 712.1541137695312, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:7": 711.8333129882812, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:0": 711.7103271484375, "clueweb22-en0040-79-05881:5": 711.6438598632812, "clueweb22-en0022-23-18726:16": 711.5856323242188, "clueweb22-en0008-3