{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "I mean the strategies to manage the transitions in and out of meetings, like creating a routine before and after meetings to help you reset your focus. This can be especially helpful in a sedentary office job, as you can use that break to stand up and stretch. Additionally, you can try experimenting and finding what works for you, rather than rigidly adhering to someone else's system. You can try creating a daily bulleted list and tackling tasks in a flexible order - without worrying about the \"how and when\" as long as they get done. Another alternative approach that might work is the \"Flowtime\" technique. It's like a flexible version of the Pomodoro method. You pick a task, start a timer, and work for as long as you feel focused. When you feel your attention waning, you stop the timer, note how long you worked, and take a break for as long as you need. It's about honoring your natural rhythms rather than fighting against them", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-31-09113:8": 714.4680786132812, "clueweb22-en0041-97-03859:2": 714.4176025390625, "clueweb22-en0010-62-07657:1": 714.4052734375, "clueweb22-en0023-55-15731:11": 714.398193359375, "clueweb22-en0010-30-18704:5": 714.3333129882812}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0037-31-09113:8": 714.4680786132812, "clueweb22-en0041-97-03859:2": 714.4176025390625, "clueweb22-en0010-62-07657:1": 714.4052734375, "clueweb22-en0023-55-15731:11": 714.398193359375, "clueweb22-en0010-30-18704:5": 714.3333129882812, "clueweb22-en0016-27-02906:8": 714.3167724609375, "clueweb22-en0011-97-14716:4": 714.3051147460938, "clueweb22-en0032-01-15456:18": 714.2891845703125, "clueweb22-en0002-36-09006:6": 714.2847900390625, "clueweb22-en0020-53-14050:8": 714.2847900390625, "clueweb22-en0034-10-11301:13": 714.267639160