{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The jockey is a pulley wheel in the rear derailleur that guides the chain in the direction it needs to go when shifting gears. It's also known as the guide pulley. There are two jockey wheels in a rear derailleur, the upper one is the guide pulley and the lower one is the tension pulley. The guide pulley helps the chain shift to the next gear, while the tension pulley keeps the chain tensioned in each gear combination. The guide pulley has more lateral play, which helps the drivetrain compensate for marginal errors in indexing. This play is not a design flaw, but rather a feature that helps the chain shift smoothly. So, when I asked you to check the jockey still has some tension on the smallest cog, I meant to check if the guide pulley is still able to guide the chain and keep it tensioned, even when the chain is on the smallest cog. Let me know if you have any other questions or if you", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:11": 713.4912719726562, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 713.43408203125, "clueweb22-en0022-60-06755:1": 713.2704467773438, "clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:1": 713.2368774414062, "clueweb22-en0026-74-04945:4": 713.1903076171875}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm a casual bike rider.", "I take my bike in the train and the bus.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:11": 713.4912719726562, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": 713.43408203125, "clueweb22-en0022-60-06755:1": 713.2704467773438, "clueweb22-en0022-23-00873:1": 713.2368774414062, "clueweb22-en0026-74-04945:4": 713.1903076171875, "clueweb22-en0026-74-04945:6": 713.1107177734375, "clueweb22-en0026-74-04945:10": 713.071533203125, "clueweb22-en0005-69-04311:3": 712.9533081054688, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:2": 712.8626708984375, "clueweb22-en0026-74-04945:5": 712.7820434570312, "clueweb22-en00