{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-norerank", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To determine the perfect length of your chain, you can use the largest cog and largest chainring method. Shift your bike to the largest cog and largest chainring. The chain should easily make this shift, and have two slight bends at each pulley. If the chain is too short, this shift is difficult to make and the derailleur cage is stretched out and almost parallel to the chainstay. You can also lay out the new chain next to the old one (ensuring that it is lined up link by link to eliminate any disparity due to chain wear) or simply count the links on the old chain, and cut the new chain to match the number. If you are using a masterlink chain, install half the masterlink onto the front end of the chain to account for the extra half link the master link provides. This will ensure that your chain is the correct length and will prevent any issues with shifting or derailleur alignment.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-91-00148:3": 714.479736328125, "clueweb22-en0009-91-00148:2": 714.4447021484375, "clueweb22-en0034-87-09834:4": 714.4417114257812, "clueweb22-en0007-14-08949:2": 714.3807373046875, "clueweb22-en0011-06-08306:12": 714.380126953125}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.", "I take my bike in the train and the bus.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0009-91-00148:3": 714.479736328125, "clueweb22-en0009-91-00148:2": 714.4447021484375, "clueweb22-en0034-87-09834:4": 714.4417114257812, "clueweb22-en0007-14-08949:2": 714.3807373046875, "clueweb22-en0011-06-08306:12": 714.380126953125, "clueweb22-en0009-38-02192:0": 714.32763671875, "clueweb22-en0024-98-15927:3": 714.3217163085938, "clueweb22-en0035-30-12637:1": 714.3208618164062, "clueweb22-en0028-57-07555:7": 714.287109375, "clueweb22-en0024-98-15927:5": 714.279968